# Shopify Liquid — Senior Developer Rules

## Core Liquid Syntax
- Always use `{% liquid %}` tags for multi-line logic to reduce tag clutter
- Prefer `{% render %}` over `{% include %}` — `include` is deprecated in OS2.0
- Use `{% render 'snippet-name', variable: value %}` to pass isolated scope to snippets
- Snippets rendered with `{% render %}` do NOT inherit parent scope — pass all needed vars explicitly
- Use `{% content_for_header %}` in `<head>` and `{% content_for_layout %}` in `<main>` of layout files
- Use `{% content_for_index %}` only in index templates

## Variables & Filters
- Always `| escape` or `| escape_once` for user-generated or dynamic string output in HTML attributes
- Use `| default: 'fallback'` to guard against nil values — never assume a setting exists
- Use `| strip_html` before character counting or truncating text
- Use `| handleize` when creating HTML IDs or CSS class slugs from strings
- Use `| asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'style'` for critical CSS assets
- Use `| image_url: width: 800 | image_tag` instead of manual `<img>` for Shopify CDN optimization
- Avoid storing large objects in Liquid `assign` inside loops — prefer direct access

## Sections & Blocks (OS 2.0)
- Every section MUST have a `{% schema %}` block at the bottom
- Schema `name` should be human-readable (shown in theme editor)
- Always set `"presets"` in schema so sections are addable from the theme editor
- Use `section.settings.*` — never hardcode copy/colors that editors should control
- Limit `blocks` per section using `"max_blocks"` to prevent editor abuse
- Use `"type": "article"`, `"type": "collection"`, `"type": "product"` pickers for resource links
- Always add `"limit": 1` to singleton sections (header, footer, announcement bar)
- Use `class="shopify-section"` — Shopify wraps sections in a `<div class="shopify-section">` automatically; don't double-wrap

## Templates (OS 2.0 JSON Templates)
- Use JSON templates (`templates/*.json`) — NOT `.liquid` templates, except for gift_card and password
- JSON templates reference sections by ID using `"sections"` and `"order"` keys
- Never put business logic directly in JSON templates — delegate to sections/snippets

## Performance Best Practices
- Lazy-load images below the fold: use `loading="lazy"` and `fetchpriority="high"` for LCP images
- Use `{% unless request.design_mode %}` to skip heavy JS init in theme editor if not needed
- Avoid `{% for %}` loops over large collections in Liquid — use `paginate` or JS filtering
- Use `{% paginate collection.products by 24 %}` for collection pages
- Minimize Liquid logic in `layout/theme.liquid` — keep it lean
- Use `| stylesheet_tag` and `| script_tag` filters for proper asset loading

## Metafields & Metaobjects
- Access metafields via `product.metafields.namespace.key`
- Always check `if product.metafields.namespace.key != blank` before rendering
- Use `metaobject.fields.key.value` for metaobject field access
- Define metafield types in Shopify Admin — never cast manually

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- All `<img>` must have `alt="{{ image.alt | escape }}"` — never empty unless decorative
- Decorative images: `alt=""` and `aria-hidden="true"`
- Icon-only buttons MUST have `aria-label="..."` or `<span class="visually-hidden">...</span>`
- Use `role="status"` and `aria-live="polite"` for cart count and dynamic updates
- Focus management: use `tabindex="-1"` on modal containers and `.focus()` via JS after open
- Never remove `outline` on focus without a visible replacement
- Use semantic HTML: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`

## Internationalization (i18n)
- Always use `{{ 'key' | t }}` for user-facing strings — never hardcode English text
- Add all new strings to `locales/en.default.json` first
- Use `{{ 'key' | t: variable: value }}` for interpolated translations
- Use `{{ 'key' | t: count: number }}` for pluralization

## Custom File Naming Convention
- Custom sections: `sections/custom-[name].liquid` (e.g., `custom-hero-banner.liquid`)
- Custom snippets: `snippets/custom-[name].liquid` (e.g., `custom-product-badge.liquid`)
- Custom CSS: `assets/custom-base.css`, `assets/custom-[feature].css`
- Custom JS: `assets/custom-main.js`, `assets/custom-[feature].js`
- NEVER modify Dawn's original files directly — always extend or override

## Schema Best Practices
- Group related settings using `"type": "header"` dividers in settings array
- Use `"info"` keys to explain complex settings to merchants
- Always provide `"default"` values for all settings
- Use `"visible_if"` (where supported) to conditionally show settings
- Keep schema `"name"` under 25 characters for clean editor display
